'' TWO MODULES THAT BOTH HAVE A GLOBAL NEEDING CONSTRUCTION LINK. Each one gets a
'' _GLOBAL__I and a _GLOBAL__D; fbc makes both module-local (llvm-nm 't', measured
'' 2026-09-26) and tiko emitted them external, so this pair failed with
'' "lld-link: duplicate symbol: _GLOBAL__I" and again for _GLOBAL__D.
''
'' THE PROGRAM IS RUN TOO: internal initialisers that nothing registered would link and
'' then leave both strings unconstructed, so 'a then b' is the half the link cannot
'' show. global-init-internal.test pins the registration in IR.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target win64-msvc tests/driver/src/global-init-a.bas tests/driver/src/global-init-b.bas -o tests/driver/globalinit.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=toolchains/tiko-windows/lib/win64-msvc
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-NOT: duplicate symbol
'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/driver/globalinit.exe
'' RUN: tests/driver/globalinit.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: a
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: b
